UnitSettlementReceiverValidation
└── when the transferrer delivers tokens
    ├── given all five source values match
    │   └── it continues to payload decoding
    ├── given a caller or source value that differs from the configuration
    │   └── it reverts with the named error and writes no status
    ├── given several wrong source values
    │   └── it reverts with the first error in check order
    ├── given a bad source and a malformed payload
    │   └── it returns the source error
    ├── given a zero amount
    │   └── it reverts with SettlementReceiver_ZeroAmount
    ├── given a payload that is not 64 bytes or has a dirty merchant word
    │   └── it reverts with SettlementReceiver_InvalidPayload
    ├── given an unused payment id
    │   └── it emits StatusChanged from None to Received
    └── given a payment id that is not None
        └── it reverts with SettlementReceiver_InvalidTransition
